{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-107754",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Let $r$ and $h$ be the radius and height of the cylinder, respectively. \n\nWe are given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{h}{r}=3\\,⟹\\,h=3r.\n$$\n\nWe can find the lateral surface area of a cylinder using the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{L}=2\\pi rh.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the values\n\n$$\n{S}_{L}=864\\pi ,\\,h=3r\n$$\n\ninto the formula for ${S}_{L},$ we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{L} & =2\\pi rh \\\\ 864\\pi  & =2\\pi r(3r) \\\\ 864\\pi  & =6\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\ {r}^{2} & =\\frac{864\\pi }{6\\pi } \\\\ {r}^{2} & =144 \\\\ r & =12\\,\\text{cm}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we disregard the negative solution since length must be positive.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
